<section class="pipeline-section" id="alerts"><div class="shell"><div class="section-title"><p class="overline">How it works</p><h2>Scheduler, check,<br>event, notification.</h2><p>A scheduler enqueues a sweep every interval. Each target gets an HTTP check and, for https targets, a certificate inspection. The result is stored as a check event. When status changes between operational, degraded, and unavailable, an incident, warning, or recovery event is stored and a notification goes to the configured channels: email over SMTP and a webhook.</p></div>
<ol class="engine-path" aria-label="Alert flow">{% for step in ["Scheduler","Monitoring job","HTTP check","Signal processor","PostgreSQL","Dashboard"] %}<li><span class="project-type">{{ loop.index0 | pad }}</span><strong>{{ step }}</strong></li>{% endfor %}</ol>
<pre class="vector-console" aria-label="Rules">IF the check fails or returns 5xx      THEN status = unavailable → incident
IF status is 4xx or response &gt; 1500 ms  THEN status = degraded → warning
IF the certificate expires within 14 days THEN ssl warning
IF status returns to operational         THEN recovered</pre>
<p class="fine-print">Targets are registered by the operator with an admin key; the dashboard is public and read-only. Degraded and unavailable thresholds are configuration, not code.</p></div></section>
